From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 04:38:44 -0400
Subject: screenshot: capture the page, a region, or the full document

Shift-Cmd-2 captures the visible page, Option-Shift-Cmd-2 a rectangle the
user drags out (Chromium's ScreenshotFlow), Shift-Cmd-1 the whole document
through the DevTools protocol from a trusted in-browser client. Every mode
writes "Stedding <host> <time>.png" to the Downloads folder and puts the same
image on the clipboard. docs/features/screenshot.md C1-C4. Shift-Cmd-3 to 6
are macOS's own screenshot keys and never reach an application.

Why: Arc's Capture is one of the things a switcher misses first; extensions
that do it want the pages they see.

Removable when: never; this is product behaviour.
